Fix meson setup failure with -Dbash_completion=false: bash_completion_dir
is only assigned when the option is enabled (meson.build:269), but the
configuration summary reads it unconditionally (meson.build:433), so
disabling the option fails with 'Unknown variable "bash_completion_dir"'.
Only print the directory when the option is enabled. Bug present upstream
through current main.

--- a/meson.build	2026-07-03 14:03:06.154798472 +0200
+++ b/meson.build	2026-07-03 14:03:06.155798472 +0200
@@ -430,7 +430,7 @@
   '    Battery/mains power detection:          ' + battery_detection_library_name,
   '    Releasing heap memory with malloc_trim: ' + have_malloc_trim.to_string(),
   '    Store creation time:                    ' + glib.version().version_compare('>=2.70.0').to_string(),
-  '    Bash completion support:                ' + get_option('bash_completion').to_string() + ' (' + bash_completion_dir + ')',
+  '    Bash completion support:                ' + get_option('bash_completion').to_string() + (get_option('bash_completion') ? ' (' + bash_completion_dir + ')' : ''),
   '\nData Miners / Writebacks:',
   '    FS (File System):                       ' + have_tracker_miner_fs.to_string(),
   '   Extract (secondary extraction):     ' + have_tracker_extract.to_string(),
